Notes
-----
certifi (MPL-2.0)
  Mozilla Public License 2.0 is a file-level weak copyleft license. certifi is
  consumed as an unmodified published wheel (a transitive dependency of
  `requests`/`botocore`); no certifi source is modified or redistributed by
  this repository, so the MPL-2.0 source-disclosure obligation is not
  triggered. MPL-2.0 is compatible with distributing this sample under MIT-0.

victory-vendor (MIT AND ISC)
  A transitive dependency of `recharts`. It re-publishes a subset of the D3
  modules (d3-array, d3-scale, d3-shape, and related) so that Recharts can
  depend on CommonJS builds. The "MIT AND ISC" identifier reflects the mix of
  licenses of the bundled D3 modules; both are permissive and require only
  that their copyright and permission notices be preserved, which the
  published package does.

caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0)
  A browser-compatibility dataset used by `browserslist` during the Vite
  build. It is a build-time-only dependency and is not included in the
  deployed frontend bundle, so the CC-BY-4.0 attribution obligation is not
  triggered by distribution of this sample. It is listed here for
  completeness. Attribution: caniuse-lite is derived from the "Can I use"
  support tables (https://caniuse.com), by Alexis Deveria, licensed
  CC BY 4.0.

Amazon Bedrock foundation models
  This sample invokes Anthropic Claude models through Amazon Bedrock. Those
